#HELPS

0 MAGESPELLS MAGECOMMANDS~
Sphere Mage command reference. This is not Sorcerer book magic.
Use MAGEPOWERS for unlocked powers, SPHERE for tracks and HELP <command>.
Each optional quintessence argument defaults to zero unless noted.
Targeted casts require Correspondence 1 for self, 2 for the same room,
5 for the same area and 6 for another area. Ordinary trained tracks cap
at 5, so a cross-area target is normally unavailable.
Targeted attacks, Mage Heal and Better Body cost their base mana plus 100 times the
square of Correspondence distance, plus 300 per quintessence.
Missing/protected targets, invalid numbers and rejected prerequisites
do not spend their resources. A valid paid attempt may fail or be resisted.
Heart's Blood supplies at most five missing quintessence per cast, causes
200-500 damage per missing point, never overdraws BODY and refuses lethal
lifeforce payments. Mana failure does not consume lifeforce.
Healing and Better Body require yourself or a group member on your plane;
they are not hostile PK actions. Hostile casts respect PK, groups and safety.
Remote magic cannot cross private, solitary or no-teleport room protection.
The caster remains in the original room after a remote safety probe.
~

0 ANALYZE~
Syntax: analyze <carried object>
Mage, Matter 1. Uses Identify on an object you carry.
It does not identify arbitrary remote objects.
~

0 RIFT~
Syntax: rift <target> [quintessence]
Mage, Correspondence 4. Costs 500 mana and the selected quintessence.
Zero quintessence attempts direct travel to the target. A positive amount
creates temporary linked portals instead. Portal duration depends on the
successful spell roll and quintessence. Player targets must enable summon;
native high-level-NPC and familiar exclusions still apply.
Combat, fight timers, restraint, spectral roots, protected rooms and
shadow/deep-Umbra/ethereal states block it before payment.
~

0 BEGINNERSLUCK~
Syntax: beginnersluck [quintessence]
Mage, Entropy 2. Costs 3500 mana plus the selected quintessence, not
300 additional mana per point. A successful roll grants a limited number
of automatically successful initial attacks. An active luck reserve
cannot be stacked or refreshed by recasting.
~

0 BRITTLEBONES~
Syntax: brittlebones [target] [quintessence]
Mage, Entropy 3. Base mana 2000; see HELP MAGESPELLS for distance costs.
Reduces the victim's actual soak for a limited number of attacks.
Without a target it uses the current opponent. An explicit target takes
priority over an existing fight. Duplicate affects do not stack.
The named affect is removed safely when its charges are exhausted.
~

0 MUTATEEPHEMERA~
Syntax: mutateephemera [target] [quintessence]
Mage, Entropy 5. Base mana 8000, plus distance and quintessence costs.
Twists fate against an eligible enemy, setting Mutate Ephemera and its
timer; it also imposes a short wait on the target. Recasting while active
is rejected without payment. Native player magic resistance can stop a
valid paid attempt. Missing targets use your current opponent.
~

0 SHATTERWALL~
Syntax: shatterwall <north|east|south|west|up|down>
Mage, Matter 2. Attempts to remove a magically sculpted wall on an exit.
One-letter direction aliases are accepted. This is not permission to
remove ordinary area geometry or arbitrary permanent doors.
~

0 SCULPTURE~
Syntax: sculpture <north|east|south|west|up|down>
Mage, Matter 3. Uses Matter to create a wall on an eligible existing exit.
One-letter direction aliases are accepted. Existing wall, exit and
native placement restrictions still apply.
~

0 ALTERWEIGHT SORCALTERWEIGHT~
Syntax: alterweight [target] [quintessence]
Mage, Matter 5. Base mana 6000, plus distance and quintessence costs.
Crushes an eligible target with gravity damage and records a timed affect.
The marker adds 3 to native attack delay before the minimum-delay clamp.
Further valid casts can damage again but do not stack the marker.
It rejects same-area remote player targets and NPCs above level 800.
An omitted target means the current opponent, not the caster.
~

0 MAGEINVIS SORCINVIS~
Syntax: mageinvis [quintessence]
Mage, Mind 5. Costs 5000 mana plus 300 per quintessence.
Creates the named temporary Mage Invisibility affect, blocking the
caster's image through mind magic. Active Mage Invisibility does not stack.
The historical SORCINVIS alias still invokes sphere Mage code, not book magic.
~

0 SPIRITSENSE SPIRITSENCE~
Syntax: spiritsense
Mage, Spirit 1. Toggles the ability to see between planes.
SPIRITSENCE is retained as a historical spelling alias.
This does not itself transport you or grant unrestricted cross-plane attacks.
~

0 SPIRITCARESS~
Syntax: spiritcaress
Mage, Spirit 2. Toggles the Mage Caress state used by native combat safety
to permit reaching a shadow-plane target. It does not transport either body
and does not remove other combat protections.
~

0 STEPSIDEWAYS~
Syntax: stepsideways [quintessence]
Mage, Spirit 3. A successful roll toggles the near Umbra/shadow plane.
You must leave the deep Umbra before stepping back to the material world.
A no-teleport room blocks planar travel. A valid attempt consumes selected
quintessence but no base mana; quintessence reduces gauntlet battering.
Crossing can hurt you. Failed rolls can still consume the paid quintessence.
~

0 BREAKDREAMSHELL~
Syntax: breakdreamshell [quintessence]
Mage, Spirit 5. Requires the shadow-plane state before attempting to enter
or leave the deep Umbra. A no-teleport room prevents the transition.
Like Step Sideways, a valid attempt spends selected quintessence, has no
base mana cost and can cause self-damage while crossing the dreamshell.
~

0 HEARTSBLOOD~
Syntax: heartsblood
Mage, Prime 1. Toggles use of lifeforce for missing quintessence.
The toggle itself does not create a quintessence balance.
The shared cast accounting spends actual BODY first, then supplies no more
than five missing points with 200-500 damage each if the caster can survive.
See HELP MAGESPELLS for atomic payment and failure rules.
~

0 HOLYSMOTE~
Syntax: holysmote
Mage, Prime 2. Creating the floating holy sword costs 4000 mana and
two quintessence. A valid roll may fail after payment.
Typing HOLYSMOTE while the sword exists dismisses it without payment.
The sword state is used by the existing native combat attack hook.
~

0 MAGEENCHANT SORCENCHANT~
Syntax: mageenchant <carried weapon>
Mage, Prime 3. Costs 5000 mana and five quintessence per valid attempt.
A successful roll gives the weapon the aggravated-damage quest flag.
Already-enchanted weapons, artifacts, relics and non-weapons are rejected.
Payment failure does not consume Heart's Blood lifeforce.
The historical SORCENCHANT alias still requires the sphere Mage class.
~

0 PARADOXWARD MAGEWARD~
Syntax: ward <quintessence>
Mage, Prime 5. Requires at least one quintessence and costs 5000 mana
plus 300 per point. A successful roll creates a reserve that is consumed
by the existing paradox-backlash calculation.
WARD dispatches to other ward implementations for other classes;
this entry documents only the sphere Mage variant.
~

0 WARD~
The unprefixed WARD command dispatches by class.
Werewolf: invokes the Spirit Ward gift; see HELP RESTOREDGIFTS.
Mage: ward <quintessence> invokes Prime 5 Paradox Ward; HELP MAGEWARD.
It does not grant either power to other classes.
Class-prefixed ward abilities and Sorcerer book wards are separate systems.
~

0 ARETE~
Syntax: arete
Mage progression command. Raises Arete by one after the experience check,
up to the existing cap of 10. Arete supplies the dice used by sphere magic.
The command reports its current experience requirement before rejection.
~

0 MAGEHEAL SORCHEAL~
Syntax: mageheal [target] [quintessence]
Mage, Life 2. Base mana 2500, plus distance and quintessence costs.
No target means yourself. Other targets must be group members on your plane.
Restores hit points from successful spell power, capped at the target's
maximum hit points. A full-health target is rejected without payment.
This is distinct from the legacy class HEAL command and the Heal item spell.
The SORCHEAL alias does not make this a Sorcerer book power.
~

0 BETTERBODY SORCBETTERBODY~
Syntax: betterbody <target> <str|dex|con|int|wis> [quintessence]
Mage, Life 3. Base mana 4900, plus distance and quintessence costs.
Raises exactly one derived stat by one for a limited time; it never edits
stored base stats. Only yourself or a group member on your plane qualifies.
Only one Better Body attribute may be active at once.
Invalid attributes and duplicate applications are rejected before payment.
All five attribute choices are implemented; the modifier ends with its timer.
~

0 POLYMORPHOTHER~
Syntax: polymorphother [target] [quintessence]
Mage, Life 5. Base mana 13000, plus distance and quintessence costs.
Transforms an eligible hostile player into a timed pig form after removing
the supported conflicting forms and held weapons. NPCs do not qualify.
Lycaon's curse and an already-active pig form block another application.
Native PK, safety and correspondence rules still apply.
~

0 FRICTION FRICTIONCURSE~
Syntax: friction [target] [quintessence]
Mage, Forces 3. Base mana 3500, plus distance and quintessence costs.
The named curse slows the target and causes recoil damage during attacks.
With no explicit target it uses the current opponent.
It does not stack with an existing Friction Curse.
~

0 ELECTRICALCHAOS~
Syntax: electricalchaos [target] [quintessence]
Mage, Forces 2. Base mana 3500, plus distance and quintessence costs.
Single-target electrical damage; NPC damage retains the native multiplier.
Insufficient resulting spell power fizzles instead of producing negative
damage. Same-area remote players and NPCs above level 800 are restricted.
With no explicit target it uses the current opponent.
~

0 INFERNO~
Syntax: inferno [quintessence]
Mage, Forces 5. Costs 5000 mana plus 300 per quintessence.
Area fire damage against legal non-group targets; affected enemies burn.
Protected, grouped and ineligible non-PK players are not included.
With no legal targets the cast is free. A valid attempt can botch or be
resisted. A failed/low-power attempt never becomes negative damage.
~

0 CONTINGENCY~
Syntax: contingency <spell>
        contingency
        contingency clear
Mage, Time 3. The selected spell must also be mastered.
Selections: brittlebones, mutateephemera, electricalchaos, frictioncurse,
inferno, polymorphother and alterweight.
Preparation costs 2000 mana; repeating the same preparation is free.
Out of combat, the bare command reports the prepared spell for free.
CLEAR removes it for free. The combat-start hook attempts the prepared
spell against the current opponent, or the room for Inferno, using zero
extra quintessence. Firing costs another 2000 mana plus the child spell's
normal cost. Invalid/protected targets or insufficient mana prevent firing.
The preparation is cleared before dispatch, preventing recursive activation
if the child starts another combat relationship. It is not a guarantee
that the paid child spell succeeds or overcomes native resistance.
~

0 DOUBLECAST~
Syntax: doublecast <spell> <that spell's normal arguments>
Mage, Time 5. Supported selections: inferno, mutateephemera, electricalchaos,
mageheal and alterweight. Examples:
  doublecast electricalchaos enemy 2
  doublecast mageheal self 2
Costs 3000 overhead mana plus each valid child spell attempt's normal
cost. The first attempt must be affordable; the second is independent and
can fail if resources or eligibility change after the first.
Nonstacking affects remain nonstacking; this does not bypass duplicates.
Invalid selections, numeric arguments, targets or missing mastery are
rejected before overhead or paradox. Recovery is 100-600 native ticks.
~

0 SPHERE~
Syntax: sphere
        sphere <sphere> learn
Mage progression for Correspondence, Life, Prime, Entropy, Mind, Spirit,
Forces, Matter and Time. Lists the current tracks and learns a permitted
next rank using the command's reported primal cost and existing maxima.
Track assignments and the existing class/clan choices are not bypassed.
~

0 CLANSPHERE~
Syntax: clansphere
Mage status display for the clan's assigned sphere.
This does not select a new clan or grant a free sphere rank.
~

0 MAGEPOWERS~
Syntax: magepowers
Lists powers unlocked by current sphere mastery.
This is a display, not a training command. For individual syntax use
HELP <command>; HELP MAGESPELLS explains shared payment and targeting.
~

0 SELECTSPHERES~
Syntax: selectspheres <avatar|personal|clan> <sphere>
Mage progression selection for an unassigned sphere slot.
CLAN selection is restricted by the existing Hollow Ones rule.
The command validates the sphere and existing choices before assignment;
it does not freely replace an established track.
~

0 MAGEARMOR~
Syntax: magearmor <robes|hood|talisman>
Creates one of the Mage's existing class-equipment prototypes after the
native payment and class checks. This is separate from temporary Armor,
Shield or Stone Skin spell affects. It does not grant an artifact ascension.
~

0 MINDBLOCK SHIELD~
Syntax: shield
        mindblock
Toggles aura shielding rather than an armor spell.
Existing prerequisites: Mage Mind 3; Vampire Obfuscate 6; Werewolf Silver
Fangs 4; Monk Mantra 2; or the learned Dragon Shield ability.
For the item/NPC armor spell, use HELP SHIELDSPELL instead.
~

0 ARMOR 'SPELL ARMOR'~
The Armor item/NPC spell gives a timed armor +20 affect.
Positive armor improves player avoidance in Genesis. NPC avoidance is
level-based; this does not claim an NPC avoidance increase.
The same named affect does not stack or refresh; removal reverses the
modifier. Existing saved negative armor affects are not silently rewritten.
Level-99 direct-player-casting restrictions remain unchanged.
~

0 SHIELDSPELL 'SPELL SHIELD'~
The Shield item/NPC spell gives timed armor +20, not aura shielding.
It is distinct from the class SHIELD/MINDBLOCK command.
Positive armor improves player avoidance; NPC avoidance ignores armor.
The named affect does not stack or refresh and removal reverses it.
This spell's existing direct-cast level restriction is unchanged.
~

0 'STONE SKIN' STONESKIN 'SPELL STONE SKIN'~
The Stone Skin item/NPC spell gives timed armor +30.
Positive armor improves player avoidance; NPC avoidance ignores armor.
It does not stack or refresh itself. Named-effect removal reverses the
modifier without changing equipment or permanent base stats.
Existing direct-player-casting restrictions remain unchanged.
~

0 VENTRILOQUATE~
Syntax: cast ventriloquate <visible object here> <message>
Sorcerer utility spell. Creates visibly attributed illusory speech from
a visible object here (carried, worn or in the room). It cannot impersonate
a player/staff speaker.
Message text is literal, not a formatting directive; control characters
are rejected. It is implemented, not an empty historical spell slot.
~

0 INTERNALAFFECTS~
Some skill-table names are internal affect identities rather than spells
that players can cast. Examples include Friction Curse, Brittle Bones,
Mage Invis, parent traits and lineage recovery.
Their spell_null registration is intentional: the owning ability applies
or consumes the effect. It is not a missing active spell implementation.
Do not add direct casts or class unlocks merely to fill these marker slots.
~

0 $~
